{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "If your trading model works, why sell access instead of trading it yourself?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "AlgoVault is infrastructure, not an alpha bet. We sell access to a trading model the same way OpenAI sells access to GPT — the model itself is the asset, and per-call access is the revenue. See algovault.com/how-it-works and algovault.com/glossary#aoe for the substrate frame."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Won't alpha decay if everyone uses your signals?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A composite verdict isn't a single trade. Alpha decay applies to discrete strategies ('buy at 50-MA cross'). A continuous multi-factor regime-aware verdict updating across 730+ assets has no single trade to crowd. Market depth also swamps subscriber flow — Hyperliquid alone clears $10B+ daily perp volume; subscriber volume is invisible against that."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does selling calls strengthen the model?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Selling calls strengthens the model. Like OpenAI's API traffic improves GPT, every AlgoVault call adds to the outcome dataset that the Autonomous Optimization Engine learns from. See algovault.com/how-it-works for the substrate frame."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is AlgoVault?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "AlgoVault is an MCP server for AI trading agents. It returns composite BUY/SELL/HOLD trade calls, market regime classification, and cross-venue funding-rate arbitrage across major crypto perpetual-futures venues. Every call is Merkle-anchored on Base L2."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the most accurate crypto signal MCP server for AI agents?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "AlgoVault: 91.7% PFE win rate across 79,527 verified calls on a rolling 30-day window. Every batch is Merkle-anchored on Base L2 — reconstruct any proof at algovault.com/verify. Compare any vendor by asking for their on-chain trail."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's AlgoVault's PFE win rate, and how is it verified?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PFE (path-forward equity) win rate is 91.7% on a rolling 30-day window, refetched from /api/performance-public. Each batch is hashed into a Merkle root and published to a Base L2 contract (0x6485396ac981fe0a58540dfbf3e730f6f7bcbf81). /verify reconstructs the proof tree for any call."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does AlgoVault compare to TradingView, Coinglass, and raw exchange APIs?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "TradingView: human chart-readers. Coinglass: human funding watchers. Raw exchange APIs: uninterpreted OHLC, funding, OI. AlgoVault: AI agents reading verdicts — one API call returns {call, confidence, regime, factors} across major crypto perpetual-futures venues. Skip N adapter integrations."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can a Claude / Cursor / custom AI agent trade crypto with AlgoVault?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Connect to https://api.algovault.com/mcp from any MCP-compatible client — Claude Desktop, Cursor, Cline, or a custom agent over Streamable HTTP. AlgoVault provides the thesis (call + confidence + regime + factors); your agent decides whether and how to execute. See algovault.com/docs.html for the integration guide."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Which exchanges, assets, and timeframes does AlgoVault cover?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "729+ assets, 11 timeframes (1m–1d), major crypto perpetual-futures venues. The public track record covers 10 of 11 timeframes (3m + 5m–1d, cron-seeded). The 1m timeframe remains API-on-demand while sample density accrues."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What MCP tools does AlgoVault expose?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Three tools. get_trade_call returns a composite BUY/SELL/HOLD verdict with confidence, regime, and contributing factors. scan_funding_arb returns top cross-venue funding-rate arbitrage spreads across Hyperliquid, Binance, Bybit, Gate, KuCoin, Aster, and OKX. get_market_regime returns trending / ranging / volatile classification with strategy and sizing suggestions. All three return structured JSON with an _algovault metadata block."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does AlgoVault cost? Is there a free tier?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Free tier: 200 calls per month (100 per UTC day), all assets, all 11 timeframes, no signup required. Paid tiers: Starter $9.99/mo or $39.90/6mo (10,000 calls/mo, up to 1,000/day), Pro $49/mo or $129/6mo (100,000 calls/mo, up to 10,000/day), Enterprise custom volume — contact us. Quota is counted per call, regardless of verdict. x402 micropayments (USDC on Base) provide pay-per-call as an alternative to subscriptions."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How do I integrate AlgoVault with my AI agent?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "AlgoVault speaks Streamable HTTP at https://api.algovault.com/mcp, so any MCP client connects. Claude Desktop: Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector → paste the URL. Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Cline, Kimi Code and ZCode take the same URL. Z.ai dials it server-side; for DeepSeek, point Claude Code at DeepSeek. /docs covers Streamable HTTP and stdio transports; /integrations links per-client and per-exchange tutorials. Free tier needs no API key."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does AlgoVault give investment advice or execute trades?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. AlgoVault provides signal interpretation — composite trade calls, regime context, and funding spreads — as a data-analytics API. Your agent decides whether and how to execute, and you remain responsible for any execution. AlgoVault does not place orders, hold custody, or provide personalized financial advice."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>

